  steps: [
    { math: '1 · The therapeutic alliance is the engine', note: 'The relationship itself — trust, agreement on goals, felt collaboration — predicts outcome across all therapy types (Wampold). Technique operates through it; without it, technique is paperwork.' },
    { math: '2 · Evidence-based practice = three streams', note: 'Best research evidence + clinical expertise + patient values/preferences. All three: research without expertise is rigid, expertise without research is anecdote, and both without the patient\'s goals miss the point.' },
    { math: '3 · Common factors vs specific techniques', note: 'The dodo-bird debate: are specific techniques decisive, or shared factors (alliance, expectation, structure, insight)? The honest answer: specific factors matter for specific disorders (exposure for phobia), common factors power everything.' },
    { math: '4 · Ethics: the guardrails of intimacy', note: 'Confidentiality (and its limits: harm to self/others), boundaries (dual relationships), informed consent, competence limits. Therapists hold disproportionate power — the codes exist because that power has been misused.' },
